{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive","id":1549411,"title":"Ananasi (Mechanical Deep Dive)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-18T12:05:42-07:00","id":1549411,"title":"Ananasi (Mechanical Deep Dive)","content":"<span style=\"font-size:28px\"><i><b>Werespiders!</b></i></span> The Ananasi are the children of Queen Ananasa, daughter to the Weaver, 'little sister' to the Wyld and Wyrm. Queen A is not a servant of Gaia, as it were, and she considers each member of the Triat to have fallen from grace and into insanity. Because of this it is important to deal with one common misconception immediately.<br /> <br /> <i>Ananasi do not serve the Weaver.</i> Their ties to the Weaver are undeniable, their similarities to her spirits are obvious, and their detached logical assessment of reality is often Weaver-like. While Garou struggle to Step Sideways where the Weaver's works are strongest, Ananasi can cross over more easily in such spaces, and in turn the werespiders struggle to cross the Gauntlet where the Weaver's power runs thin.<br /> <br /> So, what is their relationship with their Queen's mother? They fear her, they hide from her, and they pity her. While Ananasi don't have the whole picture, they're arguably closer to having it than the other Changing Breeds. A typical Ananasi may well understand that the Weaver and Wyrm are both insane, that their insanity results from the Weaver trying to trap the Wyrm. They know exactly who created them and why, and they have a direct connection to QA, who dictates their rise and fall in Renown.<br /> <br /> Given that the Ananasi were not created by Gaia, they are not tasked with a primary purpose. Garou are warriors, Gurahl healers, Ratkin control the human population, and so on. The werespiders are tasked with restoring the Triat to its former state, creating a new power known as the Triumvirate. Because this is a metaphysical task beyond reckoning they fulfil many roles. Each werespider specializes in a different member of the Triat, and has a specific job relating to that mighty spirit.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Blood</b></u><br /> <br /> Ananasi don't have Rage, instead they have a Blood pool which they refill by feeding on humans and animals. Note that this is more physiological than the processes of a Vampire. A Vampire does not feed on humans because they are the most nourishing organism in nature, they feed on humans because their blood, to Kindred, holds the most nourishment. Ananasi, meanwhile, simply benefit from blood by quantity.<br /> <br /> By default an Ananasi can hold 10 blood points. Draining a human dry (taking more than 5 points) will kill them, naturally, but a typical human holds 10 blood points if you need a refill. It's also worth noting that Ananasi can feed off of cold-blooded animals and even insects. Werespiders don't need blood, but blood is the source of much of their power.<br /> <br /> Spending a point of blood allows an Ananasi to:<br /> <br /> - enter a form of their choice without a roll<br /> - take one extra action<br /> - heal a Wound (5 Blood for 1 Aggravated)<br /> - create Strength 9 webs, enough to ensnare a Crinos form Garou or cover an industrial doorway<br /> <br /> A werespider cannot spend Blood and Gnosis on the same turn, and they can't spend Blood for multiple purposes in a single turn. So, for example, an Ananasi can spend blood to heal, or to take extra actions, or to transform, but not a combination within a single turn. Ananasi can also heal themselves of serious diseases using blood, sometimes in huge quantities requiring many victims. Remember, importantly, that you don't regenerate. If you don't spend blood to heal, you're stuck healing like a (resilient) human. Finding a means of healing without blood, like spiritual allies, or a Gift, or a Fetish or Rite, is ideal.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Forms</b></u><br /> <br /> Ananasi forms are rather alien to Garou. They may take Lilian (giant bipedal warrior), Pithus (enormous spider) and Crawlerling (swarm of spiders) forms. A Glabro-like form (Araneid) can be learnt using a Gift.<br /> <br /> <u>Araneid:</u> +1/+3/+1, claws inflict lethal<br /> <u>Lilian:</u> +2/+3/+2<br /> <u>Pithus:</u> +4/+1/+3<br /> <u>Crawlerling:</u> 0/+5/0<br /> <br /> Delirium is inflicted by Lilian, Pithus, and by humans seeing you enter or leave Crawlerling form.<br /> <br /> I would suggest using Lilian for a typical fight, given the importance of Dexterity, and Pithus for battles where you require your webs or where you need significant Strength (lots of grappling, lots of heavy hazards) or Stamina (high damage unavoidable hazards, potent attacks, any situation where you can't afford to heal).<br /> <br /> Ananasi have Homid and Arachnid Breeds. Their Metis are stolen away into the Umbra and are not playable typically. In a startling display of bad game design, Homid Ananasi have a Willpower of 3 and a Gnosis of 1 while Arachnid Ananasi start with a Willpower of 4 and Gnosis of <u><b>5</b></u>. There are no drawbacks at all to playing an Arachnid Ananasi, since they learn human skills during their initial training in the Umbra, allowing them to start with human-specific Skills purchased without Freebie points. Ananasi don't bother with Breed Gifts, so the player who chooses a Homid Ananasi is sacrificing a lot of power (9 freebie points worth of Gnosis and Willpower) for the flavour they prefer.<br /> <br /> I would strongly suggest treating Homid and Arachnid Ananasi as mechanically equivalent at your table. The only mechanical difference, if you do this, will be which form they can reflexively return to without cost, both of which have upsides and downsides. Willpower 4 Gnosis 5 works well enough for an Ananasi-only game, but might not work as well in a mixed-Fera game.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Crawling Sideways</b></u><br /> <br /> Ananasi treat the most intensely Weaver-aligned environments as difficulty 2 for stepping sideways, which they can only do in their Crawlerling form typically. Pristine wilderness is difficulty 9, conversely. Any area which is Wyrm-tainted adds +2 to the difficulty unless you are of the Hatar, the Ananasi whose work is closest to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Totem</b></u><br /> <br /> By default Ananasi get Queen Ananasa as a 'free' Totem. She grants +3 Occult and +2 Enigmas, but only while you're communing with her. Not bad at all for a free Totem, but in a mixed-Fera (Ahadi, Beast Courts etc.) game you will inevitably replace this with something better.<br /> <br /> <u><b>General Ananasi Gifts</b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Green</b></span> Gifts are often must-haves, or have applications which are incredibly game-changing, story-impacting or overall powerful. <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Amber</b></span> Gifts are solid, their utility is often determined by how likely you are to need the given effect or whether it's important to your character concept. <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Red</b></span> Gifts are, sadly, too weak to typically be a good investment. A Red Gift might have an insane cost for its effect, or have too hard a roll to reliably pass, or be entirely redundant, and so on.<br /> <br /> If a Gift's rating or function is changed by the unique circumstances of the werespiders I will make a note of it. For previously rated Gifts, please see the Garou Gifts Deep Dive: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511902-garou-gifts-ranking-thinking-overthinking\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...g-overthinking</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Balance</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Cling</b></span><span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b> (Spirit of the Lizard)</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Resist Pain</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Resist Toxin</b></span><br /> (No pre-existing Level 2 Gifts)<br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Jump</b></span><span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b> (Great Leap)</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Spider's Grace (Catfeet)</b></span><br /> (No pre-existing Level 4 Gifts)<br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Survivor</b></span><br /> <br /> It's worth noting that Jump, while still excellent, is far better for Garou. For a Garou it can stack with Hare's Leap, and with the insane movement speeds of the Lupus form. An Ananasi in Pithus or Lilian form will be far quicker than you'd like it to be, but it is never going to outrun a wolf, so the insane power of Hare's Leap and Great Leap is lost here. Cling is bumped up from Amber to Green since the various Ananasi forms have plenty of limbs, meaning that remaining stuck to a wall or ceiling or equivalent is far easier. Just keep in mind that 'strenuous' activity risks knocking you off, so rolls might be called for.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Many Eyes (1):</b></u></span> 360 degree vision for a scene. The only tell for this is that if you look at the user of this Gift through the corner of your eye they will look as if they have many eyes.<br /> <br /> Given that this costs a point of Blood, and it only lasts for a scene... this is okay, but it's a little niche. The key benefit of having eyes in the back of your head, as it were, is that you can see things happening when you least expect it. This lets you see things when you expect it. You could catch a glimpse of something behind your back, sure, and you can always pull a &quot;fine, I'll look away while you type in your password&quot;... so it isn't useless, especially given the jobs the Ananasi often find themselves doing.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Stolen Moments (1):</b></u></span> Touch someone, spend Gnosis, roll Gnosis (difficulty of the target's Willpower), on a success you steal the last 15 minutes of the target's memories.<br /> <br /> This Gift, more than anything, feels like a way to explain how the Ananasi do what they do. They're non-Gaia shapeshifters who exist everywhere on the planet, practically speaking, but are largely out of the line of sight of the other breeds. I would argue that the Crawlerling form already does this quite well, but this Gift helps too. Do note that rolling Gnosis, even 5 dice, against a difficulty of the target's Willpower isn't ideal. Against serious threats this Gift may fail or botch quite frequently.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Hand Fangs (2):</b></u></span> Aggravated damage on your hands, available in Homid and Araneid, with the bonus of being able to inject venom. Given that Ananasi venom is variable in power and we aren't even given a suggestion for how strong it should be (very weird choice by W20), this is hard to rate.<br /> <br /> Having Aggravated damage 'claws' in Homid is good however. The cost being a single Blood point works well.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Man-Spider Form (2):</b></u></span> Much like Glabro, this is the 'plausible deniability' form as it were. It doesn't really, TRULY pass for human... but what else could it have been? The problem is that the Garou have a variety of forms which are all horrible Veil-wise (giant wolf monster, giant wolf, a wolf, what the hell is a regular wolf doing here), making Glabro pretty handy. Araneid would be useful in a situation where you can't rely on Homid and you can't rely on Crawlerling... but that's a niche situation to be in. It isn't like with Garou where a Homid slipping from Homid to Glabro gains regeneration; Ananasi don't regenerate. If the Araneid form passed for human, reliably, this Gift would be much better.<br /> <br /> You can enter this form with a normal transformation roll, or by spending blood. It's a neat form in the sense that you can fight in it and enjoy +3 Dexterity without the giant size of Lilian (which is 1.5x your normal height!). All in all I'd say that this Gift is worth 6xp, and you really ought to take it when you have a chance, but it isn't top priority either.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Replenishment of the Flesh (2):</b></u></span> This Gift allows you to spend 1 Gnosis to recover 1 point of damage. Bashing and Lethal only. Yes, you need to supplement your healing, cover for the fact that you aren't much of a healer, but this isn't the way to do it. The damage you'd really want to use this on is Aggravated, and this Gift doesn't cover it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Spines (2):</b></u></span> This Gift is known as Gift of the Porcupine for Garou, and it is an excellent Level 4 Gift. This is an outstanding and somewhat baffling Level 2 Gift. See the Porcupine writeup for full details, but giving this much lethality to a Rank 2 character is arguably a very silly move! If you're struggling with this Gift I'd suggest bumping it up to Level 3.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Blood Pump (3):</b></u></span> Spend 1 Gnosis. For the rest of the scene you can spend blood at any rate so long as you have blood to spend. For example you might heal 6 Lethal by spending 6 Blood, or heal 2 Aggravated by spending 10 Blood.<br /> <br /> You could also spend 10 Blood to take 10 extra actions... if you had 10 blood, and Wits 10, and Dexterity 10. It's very easy to forget that extra actions in W20 are limited by your Dexterity and Wits. With a Dexterity and Wits of 5 each you could take 5 extra actions for 5 blood with this Gift active, which is pretty great. It's also worth noting that you can mix and match different types of blood expenditure with this Gift.<br /> <br /> So, in a given turn an Ananasi could turn to Pithus (1 blood), take 3 bonus actions (3 blood), heal 2 lethal (2 blood), web up a fallen foe (1 blood) and activate a blood-based Gift. Note that you still cannot ever spend Blood in the same turn as you spend Gnosis, including the turn you activate this Gift. An incredible buff so long as you keep drinking blood.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Entropic Bite (4):</b></u></span> Spend 2 Gnosis upon biting someone. Roll Gnosis (difficulty of 3 + target's Stamina, max 9), and the target suffers a level of unsoakable Aggravated damage for one turn per success. If you kill a human suffering from this poison they'll grant 15 blood instead of 10.<br /> <br /> The Gnosis cost is very unfortunate, since it blocks extra actions and so on. The difficulty is also going to make this very unreliable. Even if you use this to gain as much blood as possible, the problem is the Gnosis cost. 2 Gnosis to get 5 extra blood is a terrible deal!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Hydraulic Strength (4):</b></u></span> Spend Blood to boost Strength at a 1:1 exchange. This bonus is limited by your Rank, making it very strange to put this Gift at Level 4. This Gift would make much more sense at Level 2, but whatever. +4 Strength for the scene is a great bonus, and makes Lilian a much more dangerous form given its high Dexterity, now coupled with far greater Strength. With Blood Pump you can hit this +4 Strength cap immediately, which is pretty great.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Carapace (5):</b></u></span> Spend 1 Gnosis, get +4 Soak, and Regenerate like a Garou. This lasts for one scene. Honestly even if this only gave Regeneration it would still be pretty solid, that's just how good the Garou basekit is. Still, an Ananasi with this Gift will have up to 11-12 soak before armour and other oddities, which is a great start.<br /> <br /> Just imagined Fetish Armour, like full plate or chainmail, for Pithus for the first time. Terrifying but hilarious. Perhaps something more chitinous or insect-like would suit the Ananasi better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T13:34:26-07:00","id":1549414,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Tenere</b></u><br /> <br /> Dedicated to the Weaver, the Tenere are basically what you most expect of the Ananasi. Detached and pattern-focused, the Tenere learn Gifts that help with subtlety, but there are major oversights. Various Weaver-related Gifts are missing from this list. The theming is somewhat loose, and very few of the Gifts here will actually help you with managing the affairs of Queen Ananasa when it comes to replacing her mother.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Groom (1):</b></u></span> Become immune to all &quot;Appearance roll penalties&quot;, and you'll never suffer any downsides from being covered in blood, having just been through a storm, your clothes being torn, and so on. Basically you always look your best.<br /> <br /> It's very funny that a strict RAW reading of this Gift means that you keep your full Appearance when in your various forms, since Groom protects you from &quot;all&quot; penalties to Appearance. Clearly not the intended use of the Gift but still interesting.<br /> <br /> While Appearance is criminally underused, and this Gift isn't useless, paying 3xp for what will be a flavour tax in most sessions, and indeed a flavour tax which makes you more distinctive and odd, is a waste of time.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Patience of Ananasa (1):</b></u></span> +1 automatic success to any Stealth roll where remaining absolutely still helps. The Gift basically makes it so that when you want to stay still, you stay still, you are no longer someone who shivers or twitches, perhaps even your reflexes are entirely voluntary now, which is pretty cool! I wish this had more mechanical impacts, like helping with Subterfuge checks, but it's good all the same.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Beneath Notice (2):</b></u></span> Spend 1 Gnosis to make an object, or small group of objects, blend in. Anyone searching for the objects takes a penalty equal to your Obedience, which is going to be a 1-10 dice penalty. Potentially very minor, potentially huge. That said if anyone isn't searching for the object just the base effect will hopefully do the job. This would be useful for spying, thieving and so on. Make a spy cam blend in, make your tent blend in, make the car you've left nearby blend in. 'Object' isn't given a size, only groups of objects, which must be small.<br /> <br /> Worth noting there isn't a maximum duration either. So assuming that you can make a giant tent blend in, this is actually very good... if your Obedience is decent. You won't start to see huge returns until you have very high Obedience unfortunately.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Breath of Ananasa (2):</b></u></span> Giving yourself an air bubble is annoyingly niche at Level 2, but the fact that there is no Gnosis cost makes the Gift potentially worthwhile. If you're going to be out in the weirdest parts of the Umbra, or exploring underwater locales, or space etc. then this Gift is much better. The duration is pretty neat and will handle almost any situation since you can refresh the Gift for free.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Mother's Look (3):</b></u></span> See Eye of the Cobra. Understanding the Tapestry grants bonus dice here, and Sex Appeal will reduce your difficulty on the roll in some cases.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Reshape Object (3):</b></u></span> Still terrible. See the relevant post in the Garou thread. Somehow this Gift being on the Ananasi list makes it even funnier, like you need to be a truly loyal servant of Ananasa to turn a log into a shield with a touch, fear our power!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Understanding the Tapestry (4):</b></u></span> +3 Enigmas at Rank 4 isn't that great. The flavour of the Gift suggests much more than being good at puzzles, even in a game where puzzles can be fundamental to life. Sure, this will help you out in the Umbra sometimes, and with some spirits, but you don't have any Gifts to help you navigate the Umbra or talk to spirits. If you have some really powerful Gift or Fetish which requires Enigmas rolls this might be better, but it just isn't good.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Web Sheet (4):</b></u> Spend 2 blood and cover an area the size of a football field (120 x 53 yards) in your webbing. As always this webbing is Strength 9 and has 4 health levels.<br /> <br /> This is... a very underwritten Gift, like many of the unique spider Gifts. What happens to people in that area? Do you have to be in Pithus, as you'd typically expect? How do you cover such a huge area - is it a giant spray or do the webs seem to materialize?<br /> <br /> I'd much prefer this Gift covered a more intimate area with more solid mechanics. This could completely sway a battle by trapping a huge enemy army, or do next to nothing, depending on interpretation. It's also a very blunt and obvious Gift for such subtle masterminds.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Thieving Touch of Spiders (5):</b></u></span> See Thieving Talons of the Magpie. Sadly still terrible.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><u><b>Time to bite the bullet</b></u></span><br /> <br /> I like the Ananasi, they're among my favourites, but there are things they absolutely need to be able to do which aren't reflected mechanically. The Bastet get a version of Sense Wyrm which can, for +2 difficulty, pick up on the whole Triat. Ratkin get Sense Weaver.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Ananasi don't even get Sense Wyrm.</b></i><br /> <br /> Ananasi get a shortish General list, a short Aspect list, and a short Faction list. They get no Breed Gifts. No Apecraft's, no Persuasion, no <u><i>Spirit Speech</i></u>. It feels like the writers either assumed the Storyteller would fill in the gaps, or forgot to cover the basics. And say the Storyteller is left to do it. Accusations of unfairness will be inevitable. All Metis Garou, and many Tribes, get Sense Wyrm. So sure, perhaps Sense Wyrm should be easily available to the Ananasi. But what about Weaver and Wyld? Presumably they're very important to your job as well. Then there's Apecraft's; you can't have the perfectionistic Ananasi being inferior to clumsy Garou, but if you give them that Gift in the General list then the whole species gets too powerful, arguably. Same with Persuasion. Any fix a Storyteller comes up with will be guided by player expectations and won't be as well balanced as a dispassionate list made long in advance by a sensible game designer.<br /> <br /> If these weaknesses were addressed quite deliberately, if W20 explained that Ananasi can't talk to spirits since it helps them to avoid ever forming attachments with other spirits, that it's a deliberate design on QA's part, that would make sense... but it would still arguably be very, very silly. Ananasi don't really get any spirits which help them to deal with spirits, despite being able to Crawl Sideways. They also don't get anything that helps them navigate the webs of the Umbra, which is very strange.<br /> <br /> So what we're left with is some impressive unique Gifts, but none of the basics are covered. Ananasi feel unfinished, frankly, and a lot of gaps are left to be filled with Fetishes and Rites, which isn't a good approach. The Gifts available to Ananasi in Revised are more extensive, and worth carefully referencing.<br /> <br /> Oh, and no Cocoon. That alone is a giant shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T15:31:43-07:00","id":1549421,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Hatar</b></u><br /> <br /> Dedicated to the Wyrm as it once was, a pure and clean destroyer which permits new life and new patterns, Hatar learn Gifts which draw upon entropy and allow them to better manage creatures which serve the current corrupted Wyrm. The writers seem to have gotten very stuck on an angle of interacting with Vampires, however. You'll see.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Blood of Pain (1):</b></u></span> Anyone who drinks your blood becomes poisoned. Every turn they have to roll Stamina or become paralyzed for one turn.<br /> <br /> Who is going to drink your blood? And if they do, why would they fail a difficulty 6 Stamina roll? And even if they do, they're only paralyzed for a single turn. This Gift combines a weird, niche effect with very weak mechanics.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Wyrmling Kinship (1):</b></u></span> -2 difficulty to all social rolls with servants and creatures of the Wyrm. They tend to see you, narratively speaking, as a friend or someone to ignore. This Gift helps to explain how a Hatar passes as a 'ghoul' at Elysium, or a minor cultist in a Pentex front, or a mysterious ally to a Black Spiral Dancer. Generally speaking this Gift gives you a mechanical license to get involved with the bad guys and sell yourself as their ally, servant, helpless subject and so on.<br /> <br /> Even if you just use this Gift to help with social rolls against Banes (if only you had Spirit Speech!) it would be pretty great.<br /> <br /> It's noteworthy that while this Gift can only be taught by Queen Ananasa, in theory a traitor to her cause could teach this Gift to outsiders who could pass it on. Alternatively a legendary Ragabash or clever Bastet could, in theory, steal this Gift for their people. This is a Gift which could really change the game for enemies of Pentex, and sadly it's tucked away here!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Blood of Illusion (2):</b></u></span> More 'you drink my blood, you get messed up' stuff. This time it's hallucinations. Bad. Keep your Vampire 'friends' in line.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Call of the Wyrm (2):</b></u></span> See the Rank 2 Galliard post. Very good, but very obvious for the Hatar. This is the most over the top power to use on the servants of the Wyrm imaginable; I'd prefer if the Ananasi got a subtle version which draws Wyrm-tainted people, animals and spirits towards a location gradually, with plausible deniability, like a carefully baited trap.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Corrupt (3):</b></u></span> Roll Gnosis, targeting an object. Every success reduces the object's soak by 1.<br /> <br /> This is somewhat annoying as a Gift since, to the best of my ability to skim the book, W20 doesn't have rules for damaging objects. Whoops.<br /> <br /> If you use M20's Durability and Structure rules, where Durability is like Soak and Structure is like Health, a vault might have a Durability of 8 and a Structure of 10. So, with this Gift, you could reduce the bank vault's soak from 8 down to 0 by rolling a cumulative 8 successes. Neat. Then you still need to roll a bunch of damage to get inside, but the lack of any soak means you can actually get in, and it helps narratively speaking too.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Pulse of the Invisible (3):</b></u></span> See the Rank 3 Theurge list. Note that Ananasi treat the Gauntlet very differently; it's very likely that you will find yourself able to see through the Gauntlet very easily in high gauntlet areas, and struggling to see through it in places where Garou find it easy.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Ill Winds (4):</b></u></span> Spend 3 Blood, roll Intelligence + Occult (difficulty 5), every success reduces the local Gauntlet's strength by 1, for 1 hour per success. So, for example, with 5 successes you could reduce the Gauntlet from 8 to 3 for 5 hours. Keep in mind that this will make it much harder for you and other Ananasi to get through the Gauntlet unless you have a Fetish or an ally who can help you through.<br /> <br /> While this Gift is sold as helping Banes to materialize, it can be used for any number of purposes. You could set things up in advance to help a Garou pack win a battle you want Pentex to lose, or you could weaken the Gauntlet in a place where Banes will inevitably harm humans who are helpful to the Wyrm's corrupt works, allowing the mad Wyrm to undo itself.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Still Blood (4):</b></u> Anyone you splash with your blood (no mechanics given) loses 3 points of Strength, which return at a rate of 1 point per hour. This is a neat trick, but we're not given an example of how this splashing would happen. From you getting hurt? Hard to say. Assuming you just splash it onto a foe deliberately with a Dexterity + Athletics, this is... sorta weak? -3 Strength will paralyze even a strong human, great, and that's a handy trick, but at Rank 4 your serious problems relate to powerful enemies. Being able to just take a NPC out of a scenario is handy, especially when it comes to physically frail foes, so this isn't useless... It's just quite underwritten.<br /> <br /> Since we don't have concrete mechanics for how you get this Gift going, this will remain unrated. If I had to rate it, it'd probably be Red.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Burning Blood (5):</b></u></span> Contact with your blood now inflicts (Gnosis) dice of damage. Great. The Vampires feeding on Rank 5 Ananasi better watch out!<br /> <br /> Naturally you could splash your blood on an enemy, but we don't have mechanics for that. If combined with a Gift which allowed you to do so, like Blood Webs (see the Ahadi Gifts) this might be better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-18T21:05:23-07:00","id":1549435,"title":"","content":"Fomori, various spirits, and even some Garou and other Fera go for blood, so the blood Gifts aren't quite so as niche as you might think, nor are they if you play like scumball vampires do - put a slight bit of blood in a drink and give it to someone, only instead of trying to inflict a blood bone on someone, you're triggering a freakout. Or melting them, whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-19T05:55:56-07:00","id":1549439,"title":"","content":"If we had confirmation that the Bite maneuver is guaranteed to set off these Gifts, they'd be much improved. Part of the problem is that they're underwritten and are left pretty vague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-19T08:35:47-07:00","id":1549443,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Kumoti</b></u><br /> <br /> The Kumoti are devoted to the Wyld, making them dynamic creatives who bring about change through subtle adjustments. Keep in mind that like all Ananasi, the Kumoti are meant to represent their aspect of the Triat as it ought to be, not as it is; the Wyld in its current state does not fit with Queen Ananasa's designs, and the Kumoti help to encourage new life and growth through understanding the tapestry, not simply bringing about wanton chaos.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately their Gifts don't do much to help with this.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Inspire (Breath of the Wyld)</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Mother's Touch</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Insight of the Great Mother (Sight from Beyond)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Sense Motion (Scent of Sight)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Mindblock</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Nature of the Beast (Feral Lobotomy)</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Assimilation</b></span><br /> <br /> Note that Sense Motion is slightly different from Scent of Sight in its flavour; rather than seeing the world through scent, you see the world through motion detection. The Gift is also Level 3 for Ananasi, instead of Level 2. Nature of the Beast works as Feral Lobotomy, but fades at the end of the scene, making it more precise but also arguably weaker. Getting it a level earlier isn't an improvement given that Beast Mind is just far better. I would also question the utility of Sight from Beyond for Ananasi since they commune with Queen Ananasa directly on demand; if the Storyteller wants you to have a vision or umbral message there is already something far better which would be a high-Level Gift for most Breeds but is part of the Ananasi starter kit, much like Regeneration is basic for Garou but a Level 5 Gift for others.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Arachnophobia (2):</b></u></span> You roll to inflict someone with arachnophobia, making them irrationally (rationally?) afraid of spiders. This costs Gnosis, and the effects are wholly mundane with no explicit mechanics tied to them. You just give this character the relevant phobia, for a point of Gnosis, and the roll (Manipulation + Intimidation, difficulty of the target's Willpower) might even fail!<br /> <br /> Terrible. This Gift is left to the storyteller to figure out, but what we're given is very weak.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Alter Lilian (3)*:</b></u></span> Cosmetically alter your Lilian form. This would be okay at Level 1, but it's the most powerful unique Gift the Kumoti get, and it's dressup. Making your Lilian form look scorpion-like at will is a pretty niche ability. Yes, this is a sort of 'disguise' in a sense, you could change the appearance of your Lilian form regularly to avoid getting a rep, but you have a memory-removing Gift as standard and you also can change how your Lilian looks by eating loads of arachnids. If you want to go all scorpiony, just start eating a scorpion heavy diet, don't waste 9/15xp on this Gift.<br /> <br /> If you read &quot;rearranging it to suit her whim&quot; very, VERY generously, in a way unlikely to be intentional, it might let you speak normally, be more beautiful and so on. If you take the wording of the Gift literally and take that literal wording to its conclusion, a beautiful spider-person who an entire cult can see as a god-figure... well the problem is that you still inflict Delirium. If, if your ST lets you mess around with the Lilian form very freely, gaining benefits like an eye in your back or a poison gland in the tip of your finger (for mixing drinks!), this might be alright.<br /> <hr /><br /> The Kumoti have very few unique Gifts, and nothing that actually helps them with their highly esoteric work, except for Insight of the Great Mother, which is pretty redundant. Sadly they can't even sense where the Wyld is being stifled by the Weaver or Wyrm, and they don't have anything that endears them to Wyld spirits.<br /> <br /> It's also time to point out that many Ananasi Gifts just have terrible names. Breath of the Wyld worked fine. Making it &quot;Inspire&quot; just makes it entirely generic. Nature of the Beast just feels like a poor reverse translate of Feral Lobotomy. Sight From Beyond is also a perfectly fine name for the Gift, there's nothing wolfy or un-spidery about it. It's like Queen Ananasa is insecure and needs to brand every Gift to suit herself... which is very thematic and in-character for her, it's just a shame that they spoilt the Gift list for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-19T15:04:47-07:00","id":1549450,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Myrmidon</b></u><br /> <br /> This Faction are the warriors of their Aspect; a Hatar Myrmidon might selectively battle servants of the Wyrm who are lynchpins of its corruption, and whose replacements may take a more fitting 'destroyer' role. Naturally Ananasi lack the Regeneration most Changing Breeds possess, so even their most ardent warriors will still make good use of spider tactics, ambush, traps and so on.<br /> <br /> <b>Illusion of Size (Icy Chill of Despair)</b>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Open Seal</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>True Fear</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Weak Arm</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Drying Bite (Whelp Body)</b></span><br /> <br /> There's a bad habit in these lists of finding multiple Gifts which do the same thing and giving them to one Fera. So, for example, Weak Arm and Whelp Body do vaguely the same thing. Instead of picking whichever is better, or more suitable, or making a good Gift which covers a similar concept but is unique to the werespiders, instead the Ananasi get their list clogged with both! I'm just glad that they had enough restraint to keep Open Seal's name the same instead of changing it to something like Open Spider, since you don't want to name-drop a mammal in the spiders and bugs chapter.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Hydraulic Strength (2):</b></u></span> See above. Myrmidons get access to this at Level 2 rather than Level 4, making it much cheaper, but very importantly, also making it arrive much earlier.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Scorpion Tail (3):</b></u></span> This costs 3 blood points and creates a very mediocre weapon. Strength +2 Aggravated (difficulty 7) isn't a great attack. The key upside of this Gift is that the attack is entirely independent of your limbs and your mouth, and that you get to inject your Ananasi venom (totally undefined) and poison from any poison Gifts (the Myrmidon list has none).<br /> <br /> If the Hatar blood-based Gifts could be injected with this it wouldn't be bad. Still, the Ananasi list doesn't have many Gifts that work well with this attack, and spending 3 Blood to access an attack which is worse than your claws and teeth doesn't feel great at all.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Blood Hunt (4):</b></u></span> This is Pulse of the Prey, but acquired two ranks later and with a significant disadvantage. The Ananasi follow all the same rules as with Pulse, but with the following restriction; the Gift requires you to have encountered the target in the past day, or to have fed upon their blood at some point in the past. Honestly just rewriting the Gift so that you can always find anyone you've fed on in the past would be better.<br /> <br /> The takeaway is that this is Amber. If you can learn Pulse of the Prey as an &quot;out-of-breed&quot; Gift, do so.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Image of the Great Mother (5):</b></u></span> This Gift requires you to spend 2 Gnosis and then pass a Charisma + Rituals (difficulty 9).<br /> <br /> Immediately this is akin to the worst Gifts in W20, but sure. If you succeed you enter a very powerful form which gives you Strength +5, Stamina +6, Perception +2. You inflict Delirium on everyone, not just humans (though people who would normally be immune can roll Willpower, and shapeshifters who fall prey to Delirium suffer Reduced Delirium).<br /> <br /> That is a very powerful Gift, and it will combine well with Carapace. With a base Stamina of 5, and this Gift plus Carapace, your soak will be 15 base, before other bonuses. Great! But the problem is that this Gift requires a difficulty 9 roll to activate. Even ignoring that, spending 2 Gnosis isn't cheap, and the Gift has an added drawback; it lasts for one scene and after that you're forced to stay in Crawlerling for a full week.<br /> <br /> This Gift, to me, is a great example of why the Ananasi's Gift list needs a complete overhaul. Which is very sad given how interesting they can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-19T17:12:02-07:00","id":1549453,"title":"","content":"It's surprising that so many of the combat form-buffing Gifts like Image of the Great Mother or the Bagheera's Juddho form still have major drawbacks, but most of the Gifts with serious drawbacks lost them in W20 - Might of Thor no longer weakening the user, for example. That's definitely something that probably should have been adjusted in W20 Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> But hey, if the &quot;I wish Crinos didn't last as long!&quot; crowd wants an entry point... (^VVVVV^)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T06:14:05-07:00","id":1549456,"title":"","content":"IMHO &quot;Crinos shouldn't last indefinitely!&quot; is a skill issue on the part of all involved. If you have frictionless, riskless, uncomplicated battles where there is no need for the other forms, ever, then yeah. Nerf Crinos.<br /> <br /> But that shouldn't ever, ever be the case. Crinos form is the ultimate warrior form for the Garou, unless you prefer biting in which case it's a tossup between Crinos and Hispo. But Crinos is only the ultimate go-to in all scenarios if you're in boring fights where Delirium is never a problem, where plausible deniability and the Veil don't matter, where the psychology of the fight isn't being considered, and where how you fight is as important in the aftermath as anything else.<br /> <br /> Organic drawbacks, like the Great Mother form being a huge attention-grabber which could cause problems, or how it terrifies your allies, should be fine. There shouldn't have to be a drawback in the aftermath, one which will ever be crippling (next session takes place the next night) or completely avoided (next session takes place a few weeks later).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T07:05:11-07:00","id":1549458,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Viskr</b></u><br /> <br /> This Faction are judges and mystics, akin to Theurges and Philodox. If only they got Spirit Speech or Sense Wyrm or Sense Magic or anything to help them detect lies. Annoyingly a lot of Weaver-like Gifts find themselves here rather than in the Tenere list.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Shroud</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Mindspeak</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Cocoon</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Attunement</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Curse of the Great Web (1):</b></u></span> Touch a target and roll Wits + Occult (difficulty 6). The Gauntlet is treated as 3 points thicker for them this scene.<br /> <br /> No cost, and the effect is somewhat neat. In a typical urban environment a Garou might be at Difficulty 7 to step sideways, while this Gift makes it Difficulty 10! Not amazing, but solid. A major use will be vs spirits, to stop them from manifesting or from retreating through the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Minor Unweaving (2):</b></u></span> Spend 1 Gnosis, roll Dexterity + Occult (difficulty 6), and cancel out ANYTHING which is Level 2 or lower. Level 1-2 Disciplines, Cantrips, Rotes, Gifts, and sufficiently weak Charms. This is an incredibly powerful ability which will completely change the way you interact with other supernaturals. Keep in mind that Level 1-2 doesn't necessarily mean weak. Protean 2 is deadly by Vampire standards, many Level 1-2 Gifts are incredible, and if you broaden things up to include Changelings you'll see even more ridiculous powers. If you're playing crossover this Gift is even better, but it shines perfectly with only WTA as well.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b><u>Calcify (3):</u></b></span> Roll Gnosis, difficulty 7, and each success increases the soak of an object or area. The area you fortify can't be bigger than 1 acre, and it lasts for 1 day per dot of Obedience.<br /> <br /> If this works on armour, and I can't see why it wouldn't, this is pretty incredible. Use it on Fetishes, on vehicles, on crucial objects which form part of your plan, on restraints, on a cage, and so on. There's also no reason you can't use this on your own webs! The lack of a cost and the generous duration mean that this Gift, while focused on fortifying objects, has limitless applications.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Brethren Call (4):</b></u></span> This is an SOS power, or a means of summoning your closest allies. Spend 1 Blood, roll Willpower, difficulty 7 for spiders and 8 for Ananasi. For every success you get 50 spiders, and success with the difficulty 8 version calls upon the 2 closest Ananasi. The Ananasi you summon aren't compelled to come, but they sense your call immediately and can react as they wish.<br /> <br /> Perfectly reasonable ability, could have been front-loaded to help with the Viskr's role, but good all the same.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Shattering (5):</b></u></span> Similar to Minor Unweaving, but costs 3 Gnosis and works on anything up to Level 5. That means only Level 6+ Abilities, the domain of Elder Vampires, Legendary Shifters, Incarnae Spirits and so on, will resist.<br /> <br /> Game-changing, role-defining, suitably strong for a Level 5 Gift. If this were a Garou Gift I'd expect it to be Level 6; I don't mind this being Level 5 for the Ananasi since it's so key to their identity to mess with the tapestry. Just wish they had more tools to do so on the way here, like basic sensory abilities!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T14:16:13-07:00","id":1549466,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Wyrsta</b></u><br /> <br /> The Wyrsta are the Questioners, perhaps akin to Ragabash, spending their days and nights questioning their Aspect's nature, its place in the Tapestry, and pondering viable replacements. They also handle testing and assessing other Ananasi.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Beastmind</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Visceral Agony</b></span><br /> (No pre-existing Level 3 Gifts)<br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Wither Limb</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Summon Net-Spider</b></span><br /> <br /> Getting Beastmind a whole Rank early is pretty great. Reducing someone to an animalistic intelligence feels more like a Wyld Gift, in keeping with the Kumoti, but whatever; the logic of these lists is lost on me. Visceral Agony also arrives a Rank early!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Alter Mood (1):</b></u></span> Enhance or dampen a mood massively. Happiness becomes elation, despair becomes sadness. So long as an emotion exists, even a very weak one, you can massively amplify it.<br /> <br /> This costs 1 Gnosis, but there is no roll, and the only way to resist this Gift would be immunity to emotional powers, or having something which blocks incoming Gifts or provides a chance at 'counterspelling', which is very rare. Extremely solid for 3xp. Example uses would be making a frightened person utterly terrified, help with seduction or feeding, or reducing the consequences of conflicts.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Blinding Spit (2):</b></u></span> Spend 1 blood, roll Dexterity + Melee (difficulty 8), on a success you blind the target for a number of turns equal to your Cunning. Given that you're spitting you'd think it was Athletics, or Brawl, or perhaps even Dexterity + Stamina if you're feeling spicy, but whatever. This Gift would be best against a target who you can get a difficulty reduction against.<br /> <br /> Given you get some great Dexterity bonuses with your various forms this is pretty neat. I won't say it's incredibly powerful, it has its uses, and it will help out now and then. Just remember that difficulty 8 is worse than most people think, and a significant step up from difficulty 7.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Tick Body (3):</b></u></span> Bonus Blood; pretty amazing! This Gift grants you a Blood pool of 15, 20 or 25 depending on your Rank. Given that Blood is healing, bonus actions and so on, it's very strange to me that this is a faction-specific Gift, or that it isn't a Myrmidon Gift, but it's great all the same.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Blades of the Mantis (4):</b></u></span> Another Myrmidon-like Gift! Blades of the Mantis is a very impressive weapon transformation. Two of your limbs become mantis-like swords which you can launch Brawl attacks with. The weapons are long, inflict Strength + 4 Aggravated, and you make your attacks at difficulty 5. This is enough of an upgrade from biting that I would personally call this Green, even at Rank 4. The utility of keeping your foes at arm's length and safely decapitating them rather than dragging them into your face, near your vital organs, is excellent. No reason you can't slice up someone who is webbed up two feet away for instance.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Razor Webs (5):</b></u></span> If you choose to make razor webbing, using the normal web mechanics, then anything touching it takes one automatic unsoakable level of Aggravated each turn, unless they stay perfectly still. If you use this Gift on an enemy they may well kill themselves trying to escape, or suffer serious injuries in the process. The possibility of using this Gift to block doorways, make traps and so on is also great.<br /> <br /> Given that this buffs a core mechanic of your Breed and deals unsoakable automatic damage, this gets Green, despite the high bar for Level 5 Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T16:24:26-07:00","id":1549468,"title":"","content":"My guess is the missing Spirit Speech is meant to underline the difference between the Ananasi and the other Fera. They usually learn their Gifts from Ananasa, not Spirits - but Spirit Speech is such an integral tool that goes beyond just learning Gifts that I simply added it to the general Gift list. As written, they are very dependent on the Queen because she doesn't like you joining Packs and gets furious when you take another Totem.<br /> <br /> There is much unfinished or unexplained about Ananasi that requires a lot of house ruling, Gifts being only the tip of the iceberg. I added the Sense X Gifts to their respective Aspects. I allow Gifts taught by Weaver or Spider Spirits, and most that were in the Breedbook but not in CB20. I give one extra Gift at Character Creation based on spider species, because they are spread out through the Aspect and Faction lists - chances are, a player will pick something with a cool ability (Spitting Spider, Net-Casting Spider, Jumping Spider, Tarantula with urticating hair etc) and it would be silly to deny this.<br /> <br /> Venom - I go with the Nagah version (+7A damage on a successful bite), I think most do.<br /> <br /> And then there's Crawlerling form, which would probably need a full page of situational rules to properly cover it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T19:56:42-07:00","id":1549469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive?p=1549458#post1549458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Viskr</b></u><br /> <br /> This Faction are judges and mystics, akin to Theurges and Philodox. If only they got Spirit Speech or Sense Wyrm or Sense Magic or anything to help them detect lies. Annoyingly a lot of Weaver-like Gifts find themselves here rather than in the Tenere list.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Shroud</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Mindspeak</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Cocoon</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Attunement</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Curse of the Great Web (1):</b></u></span> Touch a target and roll Wits + Occult (difficulty 6). The Gauntlet is treated as 3 points thicker for them this scene.<br /> <br /> No cost, and the effect is somewhat neat. In a typical urban environment a Garou might be at Difficulty 7 to step sideways, while this Gift makes it Difficulty 10! Not amazing, but solid. A major use will be vs spirits, to stop them from manifesting or from retreating through the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Minor Unweaving (2):</b></u></span> Spend 1 Gnosis, roll Dexterity + Occult (difficulty 6), and cancel out ANYTHING which is Level 2 or lower. Level 1-2 Disciplines, Cantrips, Rotes, Gifts, and sufficiently weak Charms. This is an incredibly powerful ability which will completely change the way you interact with other supernaturals. Keep in mind that Level 1-2 doesn't necessarily mean weak. Protean 2 is deadly by Vampire standards, many Level 1-2 Gifts are incredible, and if you broaden things up to include Changelings you'll see even more ridiculous powers. If you're playing crossover this Gift is even better, but it shines perfectly with only WTA as well.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b><u>Calcify (3):</u></b></span> Roll Gnosis, difficulty 7, and each success increases the soak of an object or area. The area you fortify can't be bigger than 1 acre, and it lasts for 1 day per dot of Obedience.<br /> <br /> If this works on armour, and I can't see why it wouldn't, this is pretty incredible. Use it on Fetishes, on vehicles, on crucial objects which form part of your plan, on restraints, on a cage, and so on. There's also no reason you can't use this on your own webs! The lack of a cost and the generous duration mean that this Gift, while focused on fortifying objects, has limitless applications.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Brethren Call (4):</b></u></span> This is an SOS power, or a means of summoning your closest allies. Spend 1 Blood, roll Willpower, difficulty 7 for spiders and 8 for Ananasi. For every success you get 50 spiders, and success with the difficulty 8 version calls upon the 2 closest Ananasi. The Ananasi you summon aren't compelled to come, but they sense your call immediately and can react as they wish.<br /> <br /> Perfectly reasonable ability, could have been front-loaded to help with the Viskr's role, but good all the same.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Shattering (5):</b></u></span> Similar to Minor Unweaving, but costs 3 Gnosis and works on anything up to Level 5. That means only Level 6+ Abilities, the domain of Elder Vampires, Legendary Shifters, Incarnae Spirits and so on, will resist.<br /> <br /> Game-changing, role-defining, suitably strong for a Level 5 Gift. If this were a Garou Gift I'd expect it to be Level 6; I don't mind this being Level 5 for the Ananasi since it's so key to their identity to mess with the tapestry. Just wish they had more tools to do so on the way here, like basic sensory abilities!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Viskr seriously need <i>Sense Magic</i>, it aligns beautifully with <i>Minor Unweaving</i> and <i>Shattering</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the General Ananasi list needs the Bastet <i>Sense Primal Nature</i> gift OR each of the aspects needs its own relevant <i>Sense Weaver/Wyld/Wyrm</i> gift.<br /> <br /> I think it is better as a general gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-30-2025, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-20T21:58:16-07:00","id":1549472,"title":"","content":"The original text of the Kumo had a suggestion for venom in Pithus/Aghora - it was a Stamina roll (high difficulty for those who don't normally soak agg) that, if failed, caused temporary Attribute dot loss. Hitting 0 resulted in unconsciousness. In Ananasi, it suggests only making it a factor of use against normal humans and such unless the venom is from a Gift, and also suggested limiting the uses per day. Also, Pithus has full strength venom, while Lillian doesn't. W20 just suggests a little bit of agg that needs medical attention or magic for fragile characters to heal it.<br /> <br /> (If you're using Nagah values... that's seven levels of agg, not dice, so you'd definitely need to make it limited in use. Also, you'll start having werespiders suffer from a case of Shadowrun's &quot;geek the mage first&quot; because everyone knows that they're absurdly lethal if they bite you, and with Ananasi fragility, that means they'll probably mostly die in any confrontation if they're not high Rank Myrmidons.)<br /> <br /> It'd probably fine for Ananasi to not have super deadly venom out of the gate, at least for whatever is more resilient than a human or mage who hasn't used magick to get tougher. They get the capacity to make super-webbing in Pithus and turn any confined space into a potential deathtrap, so it's not like they're getting reamed on this, nor were they produced with the intention of being super assassins among the Changers as Nagah were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-21T04:18:16-07:00","id":1549477,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> I think the best way to show QA's controlling nature is to make Spirit Speech a Level 2 Gift for Ananasi. She trusts you to talk to spirits who are wrong, wrong, wrong about the cosmos... but you need to earn her trust first. After all, a newly trained Rank 1 servant might get the wrong idea when Falcon starts explaining all about serving Gaia and so on...<br /> <br /> I do really like the idea that she's intentionally hampered her children and that her relationship with them is more direct, uneven and boss-employee than the other changing breeds.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a> definitely agreed - I'll post my own idea of what the Ananasi lists should look like at the end of this thread.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> nodding along reading this. IMO Ananasi venom should mostly be a problem for humans, indeed, and any special venoms should be the area of Gifts. They don't need Nagah venom; Nagah were specially designed by Gaia, it makes sense to me that the Ananasi are highly competent, but that they won't outmatch the &quot;Ovid&quot; in the roles they were designed to do. They won't outmessage the Corax, they won't outfight the Garou (especially in a larger confrontation), and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-21T05:31:51-07:00","id":1549478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive?p=1549472#post1549472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original text of the Kumo had a suggestion for venom in Pithus/Aghora - it was a Stamina roll (high difficulty for those who don't normally soak agg) that, if failed, caused temporary Attribute dot loss. Hitting 0 resulted in unconsciousness. In Ananasi, it suggests only making it a factor of use against normal humans and such unless the venom is from a Gift, and also suggested limiting the uses per day. Also, Pithus has full strength venom, while Lillian doesn't. W20 just suggests a little bit of agg that needs medical attention or magic for fragile characters to heal it.<br /> <br /> (If you're using Nagah values... that's seven levels of agg, not dice, so you'd definitely need to make it limited in use. Also, you'll start having werespiders suffer from a case of Shadowrun's &quot;geek the mage first&quot; because everyone knows that they're absurdly lethal if they bite you, and with Ananasi fragility, that means they'll probably mostly die in any confrontation if they're not high Rank Myrmidons.)<br /> <br /> It'd probably fine for Ananasi to not have super deadly venom out of the gate, at least for whatever is more resilient than a human or mage who hasn't used magick to get tougher. They get the capacity to make super-webbing in Pithus and turn any confined space into a potential deathtrap, so it's not like they're getting reamed on this, nor were they produced with the intention of being super assassins among the Changers as Nagah were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points,<br /> <br /> Design wise, I would make it related to Rank. So Rank + X dice or levels of damage (and X can perfectly be 1, so Ronin Ananasi dont get screwed up). It creates a neat synergy with Rank and Gift growth without making starting spiders deadly, while giving some muscle to the higher ups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-21-2025, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-21T07:12:44-07:00","id":1549481,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><b>twig's Ananasi Rules and Gifts</b></u></span><br /> <br /> As W20 unless otherwise stated.<br /> <br /> The natural venom of the Ananasi is akin to that of an &quot;ordinary&quot; spider, in that it can hospitalize an ordinary human and possibly kill them if they don't receive medical attention.<br /> <br /> Direct contact with Queen Ananasa remains as written, but remember that she is a prisoner and has been for a very long time. Queen Ananasa has said, very firmly, that the Wyrm has no control over her and her messages. But would she know if he did? Think of this like one of those Future Fates sidebars in Mage. Perhaps Queen Ananasa has the Wyrm and the whole Triat fooled, and she's weaving a plan which will ensnare them all. Perhaps her long captivity has driven her insane, exactly like her 'uncle/brother' the Wyrm, and she has lost her way. Perhaps she is a flawed yet reasonable ruler who has a good plan for the tapestry but will do anything to get there. Perhaps the Wyrm has taken control of her and she doesn't realize it. Perhaps the messages she's receiving from the outside are being subtly altered by Wyrm taint, so while she has full agency, the information she's receiving from the outside is warped in a way which serves the mad whims of the Corrupter.<br /> <br /> In my humble opinion, all Ananasi ought to start with <u><b>Willpower 5</b></u> and <u><b>Gnosis 3</b></u> regardless of their Breed. As it stands playing a Homid Ananasi is very much a 'flavour/backstory tax', where you lose 8 freebies worth of Gnosis in exchange for no mechanical advantages whatsoever. At least with Lupus Garou the Gnosis 5 comes with a significant downside in that you can't allocate your starting points into any 'human' abilities like Drive, Firearms and so on, though personally I play Garou as 2/3/4 for Gnosis by Breed to reduce the size of the gap.<br /> <br /> <u><b>General Ananasi Gifts</b></u><br /> <br /> Balance / Cling / Many Eyes / Resist Toxin / Resist Pain / <u>Sense Primal Nature</u> / <u>Shed</u> / Stolen Moments<br /> Araneid Form / <u>Breath of Ananasa</u> / Hand Fangs / <u>Heightened Senses</u> / <u>Spirit Speech</u><br /> Blood Pump / <u>Burrow</u> / Jump / Spider's Grace / Spines<br /> <u>Cocoon</u> / Hydraulic Strength / <u>Territory</u><br /> Carapace / Survivor<br /> <br /> Shed, Breath of Ananasa, Heightened Senses and Burrow are added to the General list since they are generally spiderlike capabilities. Araneid Form is renamed from Man-Spider Form, which is a silly name. Sense Primal Nature is added since it is key to the Ananasi identity, more-so than it is to the Bastet, who are more rulers than tapestry-understanders. Spirit Speech is added, but at Rank 2, since Queen Ananasa is a jealous mistress and she doesn't want her children smelling, let alone tasting, other kinds of koolaid until she is assured of their loyalty.<br /> <br /> Spines is moved to Rank 3 for balance purposes.<br /> <br /> Ananasi mark their Territory, with the Gift of that name, using spider's webs. Otherwise the Gift functions as normal.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Tenere Aspect Gifts</b></u><br /> <br /> <u>Apecraft's Blessings</u> / <u>Aura of Confidence</u> / Groom / Patience of Ananasa / <u>Weaver's Eyes</u><br /> Beneath Notice / <u>Control Simple Machine</u> / <u>Diagnostics</u> / <u>Spider's Song</u><br /> Mother's Look / <u>Plug and Play</u> / Reshape Object<br /> <u>Control Complex Machine</u> / <u>Jam Weapon</u> / <u>Web of Knowledge</u><br /> <u>Summon Net-Spider</u> / Thieving Touch of Spiders<br /> <br /> <u><b>Hatar Aspect Gifts</b></u><br /> <br /> Blood of Pain / <u>Odious Aroma</u> / Wyrmling Kinship<br /> <u>Blood Life</u> / Blood of Illusion / <u>Bloody Retribution</u> / Call of the Wyrm / Tar Shadow<br /> Corrupt / Pulse of the Invisible / <u>Mask Taint</u><br /> <u>Feast of Essence</u> / Ill Winds / Still Blood<br /> Burning Blood / <u>Patience of the Wyrm</u><br /> <br /> Anything biting you comes into contact with your blood. In addition, I have written a new Gift for the list:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <u><b>Bloody Retribution</b></u><br /> Spending a Blood point when you take Lethal or Aggravated damage (so long as the wound draws blood) causes blood to hit your attacker, if they are adjacent to you. If the attacker has an action or split dice pool permitting them to dodge, they may attempt to do so, dodging the blood if they achieve 1 success. </div> </div> </div><u><b>Kumoti Aspect Gifts</b></u><br /> <br /> <u>Beast Speech</u> / <u>Create Element</u> / <u>Hidden Killer</u> / Inspire / Mother's Touch<br /> Arachnophobia / <u>Beastmind</u> / <u>Form Mastery</u><br /> Alter Lilian / <u>Faerie Kin</u> / Sense Motion<br /> <u>Call Elemental</u> / <u>Infest</u> / Mindblock<br /> <u>Attunement</u> / <u>Curse of Arachne</u><br /> <br /> The Changelings and Fae summoned by Ananasi default to Sluagh, and to Unseelie Sidhe, if available. Changelings of House Varich are the most drawn to the Ananasi. Faerie Kin is a rare Gift among the Ananasi, but it is learnt by those Kumoti who wish to reconcile the role of the Dreaming within the great Tapestry.<br /> <br /> The version of Attunement Ananasi learn works in all environments, with a Streetwise or Survival role depending on the Storyteller's preference.<br /> <br /> Curse of Arachne harks back to the myth of Athena and Arachne; it is Curse of Lycaon, but instead of turning the target into an ordinary wolf, it turns them into an ordinary spider.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Myrmidon Faction Gifts</b></u><br /> <br /> <u>Fangs of Judgement</u> / <u>Lightning Reflexes</u> / Open Seal / <u>Spur Claws</u><br /> <u>Flame Dance</u> / Hydraulic Strength / <u>Spirit of the Fray</u> / True Fear<br /> <u>Razor Claws</u> / Scorpion Tail / Weak Arm<br /> <u>Blades of the Mantis</u> / <u>Drying Bite</u> / <u>Pulse of the Prey</u><br /> Image of the Great Mother / <u>Umbral Dodge</u><br /> <br /> For Ananasi, Fangs of Judgement triggers against any creature which has fallen from its original purpose, whatever that may be. This includes most Wyrmish spirits, Black Spiral Dancers, traitor Ananasi, and so on. Spur Claws is insectoid, and stolen during the Insect Wars. Various warrior Gifts are added to pad out the role.<br /> <br /> Image of the Great Mother should have its main downside, needing to stay in Crawlerling form after using it, removed.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Viskr Faction Gifts</b></u><br /> <br /> Curse of the Great Web / <u>Sense Magic</u> / Shroud / <u>Umbral Tether</u> / <u>Web Walker</u><br /> <u>Persuasion</u> / Mindspeak / Minor Unweaving / <u>Strength of Purpose</u> / <u>Truth of Ananasa</u><br /> Calcify / <u>Exorcism</u> / <u>Umbral Camouflage</u><br /> Attunement / Breathren Call<br /> <u>Malleable Spirit</u> / Shattering<br /> <br /> Truth of Ananasa is renamed from Truth of Gaia.<br /> <br /> The version of Attunement Ananasi learn works in all environments, with a Streetwise or Survival role depending on the Storyteller's preference.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Wyrsta Faction Gifts</b></u><br /> <br /> Alter Mood / Beastmind / <u>Blur of the Milky Eye</u> / <u>Disguise Fetish</u> / <u>Two Tongues</u><br /> Blinding Spit / <u>Fetish Fetch</u> / <u>Name the Spirit</u> / <u>Persuasion</u> / Visceral Agony<br /> <u>Chameleon</u> / Tick Body<br /> Blades of the Mantis / <u>Signal Rider</u><br /> <u>Head Games</u> / Razor Webs <hr /><br /> This is my best effort - I imagine a few Gifts need removing! But it's a good start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-03-2026, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-27T08:11:47-07:00","id":1549593,"title":"","content":"As usual great analysis <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a>, if I have to say that everytime you make a thread it will get repetitive, but not less true.<br /> <br /> Why did you not put any opinion on the Kumo? The lower starting Willpower, specific gifts and lists seem relevant here.<br /> <br /> (They are in the p. 274 of the Changing Breed books in case that you somehow missed it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-27T08:23:55-07:00","id":1549594,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4967_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4967\" data-vbnamecard=\"4967\">lbeaumanior</a> thanks for the reminder! I'm going to cover Kumo here when I get around to it, they're similar priority to doing the Beast Courts when I was doing the Garou post. I'm planning to update this thread with Kumo stuff, and with a finishing assessment of how the Ananasi compare to the Garou and other 'ovid'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-29T10:18:46-07:00","id":1549634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive#post1549411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no drawbacks at all to playing an Arachnid Ananasi, since they learn human skills during their initial training in the Umbra, allowing them to start with human-specific Skills purchased without Freebie points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we have confirmation that all changing breeds except the Ananasi have the same Lupus breed restrictions?<br /> <br /> I would expect something like &quot;Everyone has the same penalty unless specified otherwise (like Ananasi)&quot;, but I can't find confirmation of this anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-29T10:25:49-07:00","id":1549636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive?p=1549634#post1549634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do we have confirmation that all changing breeds except the Ananasi have the same Lupus breed restrictions?<br /> <br /> I would expect something like &quot;Everyone has the same penalty unless specified otherwise (like Ananasi)&quot;, but I can't find confirmation of this anywhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 Changing Breeds has a line at the start of the Building The Beast chapter saying that Fera generally work like Garou unless specified otherwise. It's also very telling that the Ananasi chapter explicitly says that the spider-born Ananasi don't suffer from that restriction during character generation; it's an exception, and written as one, because that's an exception to how other Fera work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-29T10:55:59-07:00","id":1549637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive?p=1549636#post1549636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 Changing Breeds has a line at the start of the Building The Beast chapter saying that Fera generally work like Garou unless specified otherwise. It's also very telling that the Ananasi chapter explicitly says that the spider-born Ananasi don't suffer from that restriction during character generation; it's an exception, and written as one, because that's an exception to how other Fera work.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are totally right, somehow I missed that. Does it mean that most get the -2 to Perception difficulties in Animal form unless stated otherwise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-29-2025, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-29T13:31:26-07:00","id":1549638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive?p=1549637#post1549637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are totally right, somehow I missed that. Does it mean that most get the -2 to Perception difficulties in Animal form unless stated otherwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>So we are specifically told about the sensory benefits / penalties of the Gurahl, and the Apis etc. but some have no mention of it at all. W20 could stand to have a lot more details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T04:17:56-07:00","id":1549665,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Kumo</b></u><br /> <br /> The Kumo are Ananasi, largely based in Asia, who have broken free of Queen Ananasa's designs and generally serve the Wyrm. There are many exceptions to this, and the Kumo aren't quite &quot;Black Spider Dancers&quot; as it were. It could be argued that the existence of the Kumo, and the fact that they continue to have all of the Gifts and benefits you'd expect of Ananasi, is part of some plot by Queen Ananasa... or perhaps she just thinks that because she's trapped in the Wyrm's realm.<br /> <br /> Kumo differ from regular Ananasi in a few ways:<ul><li>All Kumo are Hatar</li> <li>Kumo lack a Faction</li> <li>Instead, they gain access to the Ragabash list</li> <li>The Kumo are vulnerable to a type of sacred wood, hong mu, which they treat the way Garou treat silver</li> <li>Metis exist, starting with a Gnosis of 5</li> <li>Kumo all start with a Willpower of 2</li> </ul><u><b>Ragabash Gifts</b></u><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Blur of the Milky Eye</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Infectious Laughter</b></span>, <b><span style=\"color:#27ae60\">Liar's Face</span></b>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Open Seal</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Scent of Running Water</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Disguise Fetish</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Blissful Ignorance</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Pulse of the Prey</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Spider's Song</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Taking the Forgotten</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Petal Float</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Play Dead</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Gremlins</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Liar's Craft</b></span>, <i><span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Monkey Tail</b></span></i>, <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Open Moon Bridge</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Pathfinder</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><b>Terrain Shift</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><i><b>Luna's Blessing</b></i></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Umbral Dodge</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Whelp Body</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Misdirection</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Thieving Talons of the Magpie</b></span>, <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><b>Thousand Forms</b></span><br /> <i><b>Firebringer</b></i><br /> <br /> Few of these Gifts would typically be available to a Hatar; Myrmidons get Open Seal for example, but you lack a Faction of course. It's worth noting that the Ragabash Gift list is far superior to the Ananasi lists in depth and breadth, so starting with the General Ananasi List, the Ragabash List, and the Hatar List (with bonus Kumo Gifts for the Hatar section!) is pretty great. That's before you consider bonus Gifts from being in the Beast Courts or Ahadi, which you almost certainly are given that you're not going to be playing a Kumo-only game.<br /> <br /> Monkey Tail is likely &quot;n.a.&quot; since you lack a tail in all your forms. Luna's Blessing is &quot;n.a.&quot; because you are not vulnerable to silver. Firebringer is &quot;n.a.&quot; because it's very unlikely that you have an equivalent to Rank 6.<br /> <br /> There are, in fact, Kumo who have joined the Beast Courts and Kumo who have joined the Ahadi, so see the relevant posts:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511902-garou-gifts-ranking-thinking-overthinking?p=1549242#post1549242\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511902-garou-gifts-ranking-thinking-overthinking?p=1549242#post1549242\"> Garou Gifts: Ranking, Thinking, Overthinking - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511902-garou-gifts-ranking-thinking-overthinking?p=1549242#post1549242\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511902-garou-gifts-ranking-thinking-overthinking?p=1549242#post1549242 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm going to break down Gifts by level and category, bit by bit. If it's Wyrmish, Fera-only, obscure or lost it's going to feature much much later, if at all. This is intended to focus on the Gifts you will actually be getting in play, hence starting at level 1 and working up. I'll be considering utility (both inside and </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511902-garou-gifts-ranking-thinking-overthinking?p=1549277#post1549277\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511902-garou-gifts-ranking-thinking-overthinking?p=1549277#post1549277\"> Garou Gifts: Ranking, Thinking, Overthinking - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511902-garou-gifts-ranking-thinking-overthinking?p=1549277#post1549277\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511902-garou-gifts-ranking-thinking-overthinking?p=1549277#post1549277 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm going to break down Gifts by level and category, bit by bit. If it's Wyrmish, Fera-only, obscure or lost it's going to feature much much later, if at all. This is intended to focus on the Gifts you will actually be getting in play, hence starting at level 1 and working up. I'll be considering utility (both inside and </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T08:51:10-07:00","id":1549670,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Kumo Gifts</b></u><br /> <br /> These are treated as Hatar Gifts for any Ananasi who get the chance to learn them; essentially this just expands the Hatar list.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Spider Scurry (1):</b></u></span> Renamed from City Running. See the Rank 1 Homid post. Somewhat improved by being an Ananasi, as you can spend Blood instead of Rage.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Shadow Sway (1):</b></u></span> This is somewhat anime-like, but that's not a bad thing. Basically this Gift lets you project a false image of yourself a few feet away from your actual body to mess with attempts to harm you. Anyone attacking the fake you will miss, anyone realizing that the real you is nearby can attack you at +3 difficulty, or +1 difficulty if they have special sensory abilities like Heightened Senses.<br /> <br /> The effect costs 1 Gnosis, requires a Wits + Subterfuge (difficulty 6), and lasts for (Gnosis) turns. Which uh... well, if you have a Gnosis of 1-2, this kinda sucks. Also why roll if the duration is pre-determined? The writing of this Gift is quite messy, basically. That said, with lots of successes you can place your duplicate very, very far away, the formula is (Successes x Rank) feet, so with a Rank of 3 and 6 successes your shadow self could be 18 feet away; as your foes chase after it you can slip away.<br /> <br /> This is handy for deceptions and for fights, but it's clunky. The Gnosis cost, the roll, the short duration, and indeed you attacking ends the effect. But I can forgive all that because... this is a Level 1 Gift. If you've paid 3xp for this, you can live with the fact that the Gift isn't perfect. Just make a shadow version of yourself a few feet away, so it seems like you've &quot;teleported&quot; a few feet, then while everyone attacks the fake you go into Crawlerling and escape. It's a pretty neat combo and I quite like it despite the limitations of the Gift, which are pretty severe.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Spittle of Corruption (2):</b></u></span> Hatar continue to love bodily fluids. This Gift gives you a neat ranged attack which uses Brawl, which I quite like since it saves you the effort of mastering Firearms or Melee. 30 foot range, difficulty 6 Dexterity + Brawl, Stamina +2 dice of Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> Given that your Pithus form has +3 Stamina, you could easily inflict 10 dice of Aggravated damage with this Gift, which is pretty competitive. It's no Klaive, of course, but you're attacking at range, with difficulty 6, and you haven't had to invest in Strength either. The Gift does, however, cost a point of Blood every time you use it. And since you can only spend Blood for one thing per turn, no bonus actions, until you get Blood Pump of course. Successes on the attack should also carry over, of course, like a typical attack.<br /> <br /> Great Gift, all things considered, especially once you have Blood Pump so you can shoot several times in a turn. The range, using Brawl, using your Stamina for damage, it's all pretty great.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#f39c12\"><u><b>Snare of Beauty (3):</b></u></span> Spend 1 blood, roll Manipulation + Occult (difficulty 7), every success gives you +1 Appearance. This lasts for (Rank) hours. So, with this Gift you can boost your Appearance stat up to 10 quite reasonably through repeated uses. This is good for certain situations, some Gifts, for roleplay purposes, and for some Rites. Just don't say you're more beautiful than even the Gods, or you'll get turned into a spider (wait...)<br /> <br /> This is neat, and if you're really into the Sex Appeal / Gender Morph powers of the Ananasi then I'd suggest grabbing this one. It does buff Mother's Look, and allow you to turn your Lilian into a &quot;Goddess&quot; for mortals to worship if you combine this Gift with Alter Lilian and Groom.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><u><b>Web Tremors (4):</b></u></span> Spend 1 Gnosis, get +3 successes on all rolls to notive people who are hiding from you. This lasts for the whole night!<br /> <br /> That said, note that the Gift only helps find people who are hiding from you. The Gift helps you to notice when you're being followed, for example, but it wouldn't help you find someone who was just hiding in general.<br /> <br /> The cost, even with a great duration, the high level, and the niche effect... makes this pretty mediocre. An entirely passive effect would be a lot better for a &quot;notice when you're being stalked&quot; power.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Megarachnid (5):</b></u></span> This is just a better version of Image of the Great Mother. The Gift is much cheaper, lacks any downsides, and doesn't have a roll.<br /> <br /> Spend 1 Gnosis when you enter Pithus, get +2 Strength, +1 Dexterity, +2 Stamina on top of the base stats, for a total of +6/+2/+5, which is amazing. If you're a Metis this Gift is very easy to use, and if you aren't, make sure you have good Primal-Urge for transformations. If you stay in Pithus for a really long time you can also cheap out on reactivating this Gift. There's no set duration, you just enjoy the benefits so long as you remain in Pithus; consider doing Partial Transformations to get any other bodyparts you might need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T14:17:10-07:00","id":1549677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive?p=1549670#post1549670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Shadow Sway (1):</b></u></span> This is somewhat anime-like,</div> </div> </div> </div>Anime? It's the signature of the displacer beast from D&amp;D. Psionics users can even duplicate it in some editions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#27ae60\"><u><b>Spittle of Corruption (2):</b></u></span> Hatar continue to love bodily fluids. </div> </div> </div>&quot;I do not avoid werespiders... but I do deny them my essence.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T14:24:08-07:00","id":1549679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive?p=1549677#post1549677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anime? It's the signature of the displacer beast from D&amp;D. Psionics users can even duplicate it in some editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suddenly 'blinking' to a nearby location, but the new version of you is a an illusion, feels very ninja-like to me. Very easy to imagine someone doing it in Naruto or JoJo or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T14:50:46-07:00","id":1549684,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who looks at \u2018Kumo\u2019 and wonders if they particularly enjoy wrestling? (\u2018Kumo Wrestler\u2019 has a ring to it, if nothing else).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-31T18:50:33-07:00","id":1549695,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a><br /> Isn't <b>Rite of Spinning </b>mandatory for all Ananasi? It is &quot;<i>The first rite learned by any new Ananasi allows her to create her Sylie.&quot;</i> So without this, they learn no new gifts, they cant even function because:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Werespiders grant their loyalty to only one spirit:<br /> Queen Ananasa. She teaches them all of their Gifts as<br /> they meditate in their Sylies. </div> </div> </div>So no Rite of Spinning = no Sylie; no Sylie = no Gifts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, can Ananasi learn gifts from other Factions and Aspects? I assume yes at level x5 xp as Werewolves do. I think all changing breeds can learn from their respective other breed/auspice/tribe/aspect/faction right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-31-2025, 09:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T02:36:36-07:00","id":1549706,"title":"","content":"Unclear! The Kumo presumably learn all of their Gifts from relevant Spirits, but I remember a line in Revised about how QA continues to teach Gifts even to those who betray her for the Wyrm (i.e. become Kumo) as part of some overarching strategy. The idea is that anything she created will naturally spin webs that ensnare, and while her plan isn't to capture the Wyrm (more replace him) it will ultimately harm the Wyrm if he takes a bunch of Ananasi as his servants, since they will inevitably place limitations and 'webs' on their peers and their surroundings, adding more stasis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-01T05:21:29-07:00","id":1549707,"title":"","content":"I think this is another example of the usual bad design associated with the original world of darkness.<br /> <br /> Why make the breeds to mandatory pay for some stats (a rite in this case), just make them part of their natural abilities and call it a day. Simplifies the resource accounting process and makes everything more streamlined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T10:40:23-07:00","id":1550944,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Antara</b></u><br /> <br /> The &quot;Breakers&quot;, Antara are formerly loyal Ananasi who choose to fully betray Queen Ananasa to serve their own whims. In order to escape QA they embrace the inevitable victory of the Wyrm, however they believe themselves to be truly free, neither serving QA nor the Wyrm. They see the Kumo as fools who believe they are serving the Wyrm but are in fact helping QA. QA believes that these rogue children will ultimately ensnare the Wyrm in their webs, and so she continues to teach them Gifts, allowing them to act however they wish and hoping that like the Kumo they will calcify and ensnare the Wyrm's ranks by their very nature.<ul><li>Antara are normal Ananasi for the most part.</li> <li>They learn the Gifts from the General, Faction and Aspect lists without any restrictions, meaning they get access to EVERY Ananasi Gift for 3 x Level xp.</li> <li>All of their prior markings from their work as an Ananasi remain; they can come from any background, meaning a werespider with Weaver or Wyld markings could be Antara and there would be no visible sign of their betrayal.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-11-2025, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T15:13:27-07:00","id":1550946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive?p=1550944#post1550944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>Antara</b></u><br /> <br /> The &quot;Breakers&quot;, Antara are formerly loyal Ananasi who choose to fully betray Queen Ananasa to serve their own whims. In order to escape QA they embrace the inevitable victory of the Wyrm, however they believe themselves to be truly free, neither serving QA nor the Wyrm. They see the Kumo as fools who believe they are serving the Wyrm but are in fact helping QA. QA believes that these rogue children will ultimately ensnare the Wyrm in their webs, and so she continues to teach them Gifts, allowing them to act however they wish and hoping that like the Kumo they will calcify and ensnare the Wyrm's ranks by their very nature.<ul><li>Antara are normal Ananasi for the most part.</li> <li>They learn the Gifts from the General, Faction and Aspect lists without any restrictions, meaning they get access to EVERY Ananasi Gift for 3 x Level xp.</li> <li>All of their prior markings from their work as an Ananasi remain; they can come from any background, meaning a werespider with Weaver or Wyld markings could be Antara and there would be no visible sign of their betrayal.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>My favourite Ananasi now. I had no idea they existed, but following you Rokea thread found them in 20th Book of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> These ones are actually playable better than most Ananasi, given the low cost of all lists.<br /> <br /> Question, who teaches them their gifts if Ananasa released them? Is still Ananasa? If so, that should be suspicious to these free thinkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-12-2025, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T16:04:07-07:00","id":1550949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive?p=1550946#post1550946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My favourite Ananasi now. I had no idea they existed, but following you Rokea thread found them in 20th Book of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> This ones are actually playable better than most Ananasi, given the low cost of all lists.<br /> <br /> Question, who teaches them their gifts if Ananasa released them? Is still Ananasa? If so, that should be suspicious to these free thinkers.</div> </div> </div> </div>My best guess is that they just find the Gifts come naturally to them, or they &quot;trick&quot; spirit-servants of QA into teaching it to them, thinking that they're pulling one over their Mother.<br /> <br /> Glad you like them! They have big &quot;main character&quot; energy I can't lie, in all the best and worst ways. Would be interesting to play one at a table or server with a permissive attitude to weird character concepts, though the &quot;chaotic neutral&quot; energy of the Antara might be a struggle for some STs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-11T16:32:04-07:00","id":1550950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive?p=1550949#post1550949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My best guess is that they just find the Gifts come naturally to them, or they &quot;trick&quot; spirit-servants of QA into teaching it to them, thinking that they're pulling one over their Mother.<br /> <br /> Glad you like them! They have big &quot;main character&quot; energy I can't lie, in all the best and worst ways. Would be interesting to play one at a table or server with a permissive attitude to weird character concepts, though the &quot;chaotic neutral&quot; energy of the Antara might be a struggle for some STs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, I just realized a Kumo that becomes a Antara is feasible, so do they keep access to Ragabash gifts? (I think yes).<br /> <br /> Can Antara learn the Ragabash gift if they were not Kumo before being set free? (I think no).<br /> <br /> Aaaaaand I am certain, but would like confirmation, that Antara can learn the new Kumo gifts (they should be able, those gifts count as Hatar for learning purposes).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They should lose the Free Totem Ananasa, otherwise it is all upside no downside for these spiders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 05-11-2025, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-12T05:06:22-07:00","id":1550952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1549411-ananasi-mechanical-deep-dive?p=1550950#post1550950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They should lose the Free Totem Ananasa, otherwise it is all upside no downside for these spiders.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation was always that 'betraying Ananasa' involved taking a different patron Totem, since it's something she explicitly forbids. You can probably lose her support by breaking the other rules often enough, but that one is the big no-no.<br /> <br /> Antara probably would petition their new patron (or its servants) directly for Gifts since I doubt most Spirits would care to teach them to non-Gaian shifters, although there's always a big enough bribe or even threat to force them. I'd guess an Antara's access to the 'full' Gift list is for all purposes limited by the contracts they can strike with other Spirits and their overlap with Ananasi Gifts. A Totem like Trapdoor Spider comes to mind.<br /> Although rare among other Fera, they can also teach Gifts to each other. Given their independent mindset, this may be the preferred method.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508